18:56:23 [ecd8] - sophie should appear by name in the story (not just "she" / "he"), so WHO-questions are answerable.
18:56:23 [ecd8] - Use observable facts only (who is there, where they are, what they are doing, what they see/find) — even imaginative characters must do concrete, observable things so the questions are answerable.
18:56:23 [ecd8] - Do NOT invent moral lessons, internal monologue, or three-act structure. Keep it to the corpus style.
