19:15:00 [0d1d] - advanced conjunction (More complex conjunction structures): e.g. while, although, before, after
19:15:00 [0d1d] - auxiliary verbs (Helping verbs): e.g. is, are, was, were, has, have
19:15:00 [0d1d] - copula verbs (Linking verbs): e.g. is, am, are, was, were
19:15:00 [0d1d] - verb tense concepts (Past, present, future, and progressive tense usage): e.g. I play, I played, I will play, I am playing
19:15:00 [0d1d] - causal explanation language (Language forms used to explain cause-effect relationships.): e.g. because, so, if...then, that happened because...
19:15:00 [0d1d] - narrative sequence language (Language forms used to organize story events and sequences.): e.g. first, then, next, after that, finally
19:15:00 [0d1d] - perspective taking language (Language forms used to discuss thoughts, feelings, beliefs, and perspectives.): e.g. he thinks, she feels, they know, I wonder, maybe
